  "hero": "<section class=\"mm-hero\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">MODEL MONITORING · VISUAL STUDY</span><h2>Keep checking predictions after deployment.</h2><p>Learn how MLOps teams track data, outcomes and service health, identify drift, handle delayed labels and investigate safely before updating models.</p><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh0 mmd0\"><title id=\"mmh0\">Deployed models need an ongoing feedback loop</title><desc id=\"mmd0\">A four-stage model monitoring workflow observes live requests, measures data quality and drift, evaluates labeled outcomes, and investigates before releases.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">MODEL MONITORING · MLOPS</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">Deployed models need an ongoing feedback loop</text><rect x=\"29\" y=\"115\" width=\"942\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><rect x=\"47\" y=\"162\" width=\"212\" height=\"113\" fill=\"#eaf7fb\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"153\" y=\"201\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#3c8497\">LIVE REQUESTS</text><text x=\"153\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Features + scores</text><rect x=\"279\" y=\"162\" width=\"212\" height=\"113\" fill=\"#ebf8f1\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"385\" y=\"201\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#328978\">OBSERVE</text><text x=\"385\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Drift + quality</text><rect x=\"511\" y=\"162\" width=\"212\" height=\"113\" fill=\"#f1f3fd\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"617\" y=\"201\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#6479a2\">EVALUATE</text><text x=\"617\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Outcomes later</text><rect x=\"743\" y=\"162\" width=\"209\" height=\"113\" fill=\"#fff3e8\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"847.5\" y=\"201\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#b67d54\">RESPOND</text><text x=\"847.5\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Investigate first</text><line x1=\"261\" y1=\"216\" x2=\"275\" y2=\"216\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M265 207L275 216L265 225\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"493\" y1=\"216\" x2=\"507\" y2=\"216\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M497 207L507 216L497 225\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"725\" y1=\"216\" x2=\"739\" y2=\"216\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M729 207L739 216L729 225\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" fill=\"#51788a\">Data health</text><text x=\"284\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" fill=\"#51788a\">Behavior changes</text><text x=\"523\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" fill=\"#51788a\">Observed quality</text><text x=\"756\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"750\" fill=\"#51788a\">Safe deployment</text></svg></div><p class=\"mm-note\">Illustrative operational monitoring loop, not live telemetry.</p></section>",
  "questions": [
    {
      "stem": "What is Model Monitoring in MLOps, and why is it necessary even when a Machine Learning model performed well during offline evaluation?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Continuous model health",
      "options": [
        "Model Monitoring checks prediction accuracy when production labels arrive, while treating invalid inputs and endpoint outages as unrelated tasks. Strong offline performance remains a sufficient guarantee until labeled accuracy begins falling.",
        "Model Monitoring tracks deployed inputs, predictions, service reliability, and measured quality when true outcomes arrive. It detects changes or failures that a strong offline evaluation cannot rule out.",
        "Model Monitoring compares new feature averages with the training baseline and retrains automatically after every distribution change. Once a shift is found, investigating prediction quality or operational impact is unnecessary.",
        "Model Monitoring watches request counts, infrastructure errors and prediction latency after deployment. If these service metrics remain stable, it is safe to assume the model's answers are still correct."
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Model Monitoring means observing a deployed model's inputs, outputs, service health and prediction quality over time. A strong offline score only describes how the model behaved on earlier evaluation data; real conditions can change. Imagine a grocery demand model deployed before a major local festival. It may answer requests quickly while its forecasts become less useful. Monitoring helps detect changes, investigate their causes and decide whether action is needed.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 01 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh1 mmd1\"><title id=\"mmh1\">A launch score cannot guarantee tomorrow's quality</title><desc id=\"mmd1\">Offline test performance, changing production conditions, and continuous monitoring are distinct phases.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">01 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">A launch score cannot guarantee tomorrow's quality</text><rect x=\"29\" y=\"113\" width=\"938\" height=\"259\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><rect x=\"53\" y=\"160\" width=\"287\" height=\"115\" fill=\"#ebf7fc\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"196.5\" y=\"199\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#41849a\">BEFORE LAUNCH</text><text x=\"196.5\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Offline quality: 92%</text><rect x=\"358\" y=\"160\" width=\"287\" height=\"115\" fill=\"#fff1e7\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"501.5\" y=\"199\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#b87d52\">AFTER LAUNCH</text><text x=\"501.5\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Demand patterns shift</text><rect x=\"663\" y=\"160\" width=\"287\" height=\"115\" fill=\"#ecf8f0\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"806.5\" y=\"199\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2c8a77\">MONITOR DAILY</text><text x=\"806.5\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#567a87\">Catch changing errors</text><line x1=\"342\" y1=\"217\" x2=\"353\" y2=\"217\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M343 208L353 217L343 226\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"647\" y1=\"217\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"217\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M648 208L658 217L648 226\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"65\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"740\" fill=\"#567c8b\">A healthy endpoint can still produce less useful predictions.</text></svg></div><p class=\"mm-note\">A good offline score is a starting point, not permanent evidence of live quality.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "Which data-quality, drift, predictive-performance and operational metrics should Model Monitoring track, and why is one metric insufficient?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Model health signals",
      "options": [
        "Track prediction confidence and changes in input distributions, using confidence as a direct substitute for actual prediction accuracy. If confidence scores stay stable, service errors and labeled outcomes need no separate monitoring.",
        "Track missing input fields, inference latency and measured accuracy when labels become available, but omit prediction distribution changes. Stable measured accuracy on labeled cases proves the whole current user population remains unchanged.",
        "Track server uptime, average prediction latency and a global accuracy score to assess overall health. Input schema failures and subgroup performance matter only when one of those three indicators fails.",
        "Track input validity, feature and prediction drift, labeled performance when outcomes arrive, and service metrics such as latency and errors. Each signal detects problems that the others may not reveal."
      ],
      "answer": "d",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> A dashboard should cover data quality (missing or invalid features), drift (changing inputs or outputs), predictive performance once true labels arrive, and operations (latency, errors and availability). Each answers a different question. For a courier arrival-time model, stable response speed does not mean estimated delivery times are still correct. Likewise, accuracy on labeled cases may hide a new population with few known outcomes. Segment checks provide another useful view.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 02 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh2 mmd2\"><title id=\"mmh2\">Model health needs more than one chart</title><desc id=\"mmd2\">Four monitoring panels track input validation, data and prediction shifts, observed labeled accuracy, and endpoint latency.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">02 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">Model health needs more than one chart</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"110\" width=\"937\" height=\"274\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#508095\">FOUR DIFFERENT SIGNAL FAMILIES</text><rect x=\"52\" y=\"173\" width=\"427\" height=\"88\" fill=\"#edf8fb\" stroke=\"#d5e6e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"199\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#387f97\">INPUT HEALTH</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"790\" fill=\"#365f72\">Missing fields: 8%</text><text x=\"459\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"610\" fill=\"#5e7f8c\">Schema · null rate</text><rect x=\"513\" y=\"173\" width=\"427\" height=\"88\" fill=\"#edf9f1\" stroke=\"#d5e6e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"530\" y=\"199\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e8b77\">DRIFT</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"790\" fill=\"#365f72\">Scores have shifted</text><text x=\"920\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"610\" fill=\"#5e7f8c\">Inputs · outputs</text><rect x=\"52\" y=\"272\" width=\"427\" height=\"88\" fill=\"#f3f3fd\" stroke=\"#d5e6e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"298\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#6979a3\">MODEL QUALITY</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"327\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"790\" fill=\"#365f72\">Accuracy: 78%</text><text x=\"459\" y=\"348\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"610\" fill=\"#5e7f8c\">Only with labels</text><rect x=\"513\" y=\"272\" width=\"427\" height=\"88\" fill=\"#fff3e9\" stroke=\"#d5e6e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"530\" y=\"298\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#b87e53\">SERVICE HEALTH</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"327\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"790\" fill=\"#365f72\">p95 latency: 420 ms</text><text x=\"920\" y=\"348\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"610\" fill=\"#5e7f8c\">Errors · uptime</text></svg></div><p class=\"mm-note\">Feature drift, performance and service health answer different operational questions.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How do Data Drift, Concept Drift and Training-Serving Skew differ, and what evidence helps an MLOps team distinguish them?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Three types of change",
      "options": [
        "Data drift changes input distributions; concept drift changes how inputs relate to real outcomes; training-serving skew means a mismatch between training and live feature processing. Labels help investigate concept drift.",
        "Data drift means true labels change without input variation, concept drift means a field changes format, and training-serving skew means request traffic increases. All three can be confirmed using input statistics alone.",
        "Data drift means model weights change after release, concept drift means new input columns appear, and training-serving skew means latency becomes unstable. Monitoring input distributions is enough to identify every case.",
        "Data drift occurs only after predictive accuracy decreases, concept drift occurs only when predicted scores change distribution, and training-serving skew can be established solely from comparing observed labels across recent weeks."
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Data drift is a change in the distribution of model inputs. Concept drift means the relationship between inputs and actual outcomes has changed. Training-serving skew means production feature values or transformations differ from training. For a lending model, younger applicants may cause data drift; changing repayment behavior among otherwise similar applicants may indicate concept drift; and salary stored in different units can create skew. Feature drift alone cannot prove concept drift—true outcomes help establish whether the relationship changed.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 03 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh3 mmd3\"><title id=\"mmh3\">Input drift, concept drift, and serving skew differ</title><desc id=\"mmd3\">Two-window feature histograms and key conditions show input distribution shifts, changing input-to-label relationships, and train-serving representation mismatch.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">03 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">Input drift, concept drift, and serving skew differ</text><rect x=\"29\" y=\"114\" width=\"302\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#eef8fc\" stroke=\"#d7e7ea\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"49\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#3f8599\">DATA DRIFT</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"181\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"730\" fill=\"#4b7182\">P(X) changes</text><line x1=\"61\" y1=\"317\" x2=\"303\" y2=\"317\" stroke=\"#bcd1d9\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><rect x=\"67\" y=\"277\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"84\" y=\"302\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"113\" y=\"257\" width=\"16\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"130\" y=\"287\" width=\"16\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"159\" y=\"232\" width=\"16\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"257\" width=\"16\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"205\" y=\"257\" width=\"16\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"222\" y=\"237\" width=\"16\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"292\" width=\"16\" height=\"25\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"268\" y=\"237\" width=\"16\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"48\" y=\"354\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"640\" fill=\"#577787\">Inputs shift over time</text><rect x=\"349\" y=\"114\" width=\"302\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#ebf8f0\" stroke=\"#d7e7ea\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"369\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#308a74\">CONCEPT DRIFT</text><text x=\"369\" y=\"181\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"730\" fill=\"#4b7182\">P(Y | X) changes</text><line x1=\"381\" y1=\"317\" x2=\"623\" y2=\"317\" stroke=\"#bcd1d9\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><rect x=\"387\" y=\"277\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"404\" y=\"277\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"433\" y=\"257\" width=\"16\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"450\" y=\"257\" width=\"16\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#dda074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"479\" y=\"232\" width=\"16\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#79b7c5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"496\" y=\"232\" width=\"16\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#dda