    {
      "stem": "How should Model Monitoring evaluate predictions when true labels arrive later or only for some requests, and why does label coverage matter?",
      "tag": "Medium · Delayed labels",
      "options": [
        "Calculate accuracy immediately by counting every prediction without an observed label as an incorrect result. This is conservative and avoids falsely claiming success, while ensuring every request contributes to the evaluation metric.",
        "Wait until all outcomes are known, then pair predictions with labels according to row position in the latest export. This produces unbiased performance even when some requests have been dropped or delayed.",
        "Log predictions with stable IDs and timestamps, then join verified outcomes to their matching records. Measure accuracy on labeled cases, and report coverage and possible selection bias.",
        "Use average prediction confidence as observed accuracy until true outcomes arrive, and stop reporting accuracy once labels become incomplete. Stable confidence indicates the missing outcomes cannot bias the reported model quality."
      ],
      "answer": "c",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Store a prediction with its event ID and timestamp, then join the real outcome when it becomes available. Compute observed performance only where genuine labels exist; also report label coverage and potential selection bias. Imagine a hospital appointment no-show model: actual attendance cannot be confirmed until the appointment occurs. In the diagram, just two of three predictions have known outcomes, giving observed accuracy 1/2 and coverage 2/3. Missing labels must never be treated as known negatives.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 04 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh4 mmd4\"><title id=\"mmh4\">Ground truth arrives after the prediction</title><desc id=\"mmd4\">An outcome delay timeline shows predictions A B C with two arrived outcome labels, producing observed accuracy 50 percent and coverage two thirds.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">04 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">Ground truth arrives after the prediction</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"114\" width=\"939\" height=\"266\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"56\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#4e7d92\">LINK LATER LABELS BACK TO THE ORIGINAL REQUEST</text><line x1=\"116\" y1=\"213\" x2=\"889\" y2=\"213\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M879 204L889 213L879 222\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"213\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dba071\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#4d7b8e\">DAY 0</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"254\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#577b89\">Prediction logged</text><circle cx=\"494\" cy=\"213\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dba071\"/><text x=\"494\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#4d7b8e\">DAY 5</text><text x=\"494\" y=\"254\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#577b89\">Outcome arrives</text><circle cx=\"887\" cy=\"213\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#dba071\"/><text x=\"887\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#4d7b8e\">DAY 6</text><text x=\"887\" y=\"254\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#577b89\">Join by ID</text><rect x=\"59\" y=\"280\" width=\"384\" height=\"72\" fill=\"#edf7fc\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><rect x=\"488\" y=\"280\" width=\"453\" height=\"72\" fill=\"#eaf8ef\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"77\" y=\"307\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"840\" fill=\"#377f93\">Predictions: A, B, C</text><text x=\"77\" y=\"337\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"650\" fill=\"#5d7e8c\">3 logged cases</text><text x=\"505\" y=\"307\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"840\" fill=\"#2f8877\">Outcomes: A and B</text><text x=\"505\" y=\"337\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"740\" fill=\"#4f7785\">Accuracy: 1/2  ·  coverage: 2/3</text></svg></div><p class=\"mm-note\">Evaluation needs event-level joins, observation delays, coverage and representativeness checks.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How can a small Python Model Monitoring job detect feature shifts and calculate observed accuracy without treating drift as proof of prediction failure?",
      "tag": "Medium · Python monitoring example",
      "options": [
        "Replace the historical baseline with each new batch of live feature values before computing change scores. Assume every request without a confirmed label is negative so the reported accuracy includes all observed predictions.",
        "Compare recent feature values with a fixed reference; a large shift triggers investigation, not proof of failure. Separately match predictions to available labels and report observed accuracy with coverage.",
        "Measure prediction accuracy by comparing model outputs with one another, since ground-truth outcomes might be late. Then use that computed accuracy to set drift alert thresholds, proving when the model becomes incorrect.",
        "Compute a feature-shift statistic using live and historical measurements, then use the drift number as the model error rate. Separate true labels are unnecessary because distribution change itself establishes prediction failure."
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> A simple monitoring script compares recent feature values with an earlier reference and flags large shifts for investigation. It separately calculates observed accuracy only where true labels are available. The 10-line Python example reports a standardized shift of 4.95, an illustrative alert threshold of 2, observed accuracy 50%, and label coverage 2/3. For a cold-room temperature sensor, a shifted reading pattern could signal a data issue, while matched outcomes are needed to confirm actual prediction quality. Real alert thresholds must be calibrated.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 05 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh5 mmd5\"><title id=\"mmh5\">A feature shift is not the same as an error</title><desc id=\"mmd5\">Recent sensor features shift against a historical reference; a standardized mean difference of 4.95 triggers an illustrative alert while only two of three predictions have labels.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">05 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">A feature shift is not the same as an error</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"936\" height=\"265\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#517e90\">COMPARE A FROZEN BASELINE WITH A RECENT WINDOW</text><line x1=\"91\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"91\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#e2edf0\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><circle cx=\"91\" cy=\"275\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#3b98af\"/><circle cx=\"91\" cy=\"223\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e4a16c\"/><line x1=\"178\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"178\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#e2edf0\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><circle cx=\"178\" cy=\"266\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#3b98af\"/><circle cx=\"178\" cy=\"214\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e4a16c\"/><line x1=\"265\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"265\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#e2edf0\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><circle cx=\"265\" cy=\"257\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#3b98af\"/><circle cx=\"265\" cy=\"205\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e4a16c\"/><line x1=\"352\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#e2edf0\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><circle cx=\"352\" cy=\"248\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#3b98af\"/><circle cx=\"352\" cy=\"196\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e4a16c\"/><line x1=\"439\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"439\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#e2edf0\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><circle cx=\"439\" cy=\"239\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#3b98af\"/><circle cx=\"439\" cy=\"187\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e4a16c\"/><text x=\"59\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"730\" fill=\"#41809a\">Baseline [48,49,50,51,52]</text><text x=\"59\" y=\"352\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"730\" fill=\"#b97d55\">Recent [55,56,57,58,59]</text><rect x=\"526\" y=\"162\" width=\"406\" height=\"185\" fill=\"#eaf8f1\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"548\" y=\"201\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"840\" fill=\"#477c8b\">Standardized shift</text><text x=\"548\" y=\"249\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"870\" fill=\"#268a7a\">4.95 &gt; 2.0</text><text x=\"548\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"740\" fill=\"#3a8078\">Investigate this alert</text><text x=\"548\" y=\"319\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"650\" fill=\"#5c7d8c\">Labels observed: 2 of 3</text></svg></div><div class=\"mm-code\"><div class=\"mm-code-head\">Python · Standard library · 10 executable lines</div><pre style=\"background:#1e1e1e;color:#eff8ff;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre\"><code style=\"background:transparent!important;color:#eff8ff!important;border:0!important;padding:0!important;display:block;font:inherit;white-space:pre\">from statistics import mean, pstdev\nbaseline = [48, 49, 50, 51, 52]\nrecent = [55, 56, 57, 58, 59]\npredictions = {'a': 1, 'b': 0, 'c': 1}\narrived_labels = {'a': 1, 'b': 1}\nshift = abs(mean(recent) - mean(baseline)) / pstdev(baseline)\nmatched = predictions.keys() &amp; arrived_labels.keys()\naccuracy = sum(predictions[k] == arrived_labels[k] for k in matched) / len(matched) if matched else None\nprint('Illustrative feature alert:', shift &gt; 2, 'shift:', round(shift, 2))\nprint('Observed labeled accuracy:', accuracy, 'coverage:', f'{len(matched)}/{len(predictions)}')</code></pre></div><p class=\"mm-note\">The code uses standard Python; its alert threshold is illustrative, not a production default.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How should drift statistics, comparison windows, sample sizes and alert thresholds be designed to detect meaningful issues without too many false alarms?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Drift signal design",
      "options": [
        "Apply a universal drift threshold to every feature and user group, triggering a page whenever a statistical test returns significance. Sample counts and seasonal variation do not matter after the statistic is standardized.",
        "Replace the reference distribution continuously with the latest observations, then alert on any difference between consecutive samples. This provides a stable, comparable baseline and eliminates false positives during normal seasonal changes.",
        "Track only global prediction-score averages rather than subgroup or feature distributions, since unchanged aggregate outputs prove all inputs and underlying input-to-outcome relationships stayed stable, including for small user populations.",
        "Compare representative baseline and recent windows, check important features and population segments, and calibrate thresholds to sample size and expected variation. Investigate business impact before escalating an alert."
      ],
      "answer": "d",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Drift tests and distances compare recent inputs against a meaningful reference, but the monitoring window, sample size, seasonality and number of checks affect false alarms. Tune thresholds against normal variation and the cost of missing real problems. For an online retailer, holiday returns can change the item mix even when the model still works well. Review affected categories, labels and business impact before retraining. Statistical shift is a clue, not a diagnosis.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 06 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh6 mmd6\"><title id=\"mmh6\">Drift alert thresholds need context</title><desc id=\"mmd6\">The baseline and recent feature histograms differ; statistical alerting must account for normal seasonality, sample size and individual segments.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">06 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">Drift alert thresholds need context</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"939\" height=\"269\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#517d93\">TWO DISTRIBUTIONS · SIX VALUE BINS</text><rect x=\"73\" y=\"262\" width=\"22\" height=\"64\" fill=\"#6eafc3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"97\" y=\"310\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#e1a074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"143\" y=\"226\" width=\"22\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#6eafc3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"167\" y=\"290\" width=\"22\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#e1a074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"213\" y=\"218\" width=\"22\" height=\"108\" fill=\"#6eafc3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"237\" y=\"266\" width=\"22\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#e1a074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"283\" y=\"250\" width=\"22\" height=\"76\" fill=\"#6eafc3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"307\" y=\"230\" width=\"22\" height=\"96\" fill=\"#e1a074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"353\" y=\"286\" width=\"22\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#6eafc3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"377\" y=\"226\" width=\"22\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#e1a074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"423\" y=\"306\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#6eafc3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"447\" y=\"246\" width=\"22\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#e1a074\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"63\" y1=\"328\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"328\" stroke=\"#8ca5b4\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"74\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"770\" fill=\"#3e819b\">Baseline</text><text x=\"209\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"770\" fill=\"#b78054\">Recent</text><rect x=\"540\" y=\"158\" width=\"404\" height=\"202\" fill=\"#ecf9f2\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"558\" y=\"193\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"840\" fill=\"#318d75\">BEFORE YOU PAGE AN ENGINEER</text><circle cx=\"563\" cy=\"223\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#3a9c87\"/><text x=\"581\" y=\"229\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#476d7e\">Compare appropriate time windows</text><circle cx=\"563\" cy=\"257\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#3a9c87\"/><text x=\"581\" y=\"263\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#476d7e\">Check sample size and seasonality</text><circle cx=\"563\" cy=\"291\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#3a9c87\"/><text x=\"581\" y=\"297\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#476d7e\">Review affected customer segments</text><circle cx=\"563\" cy=\"325\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#3a9c87\"/><text x=\"581\" y=\"331\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#476d7e\">Calibrate thresholds to impact</text></svg></div><p class=\"mm-note\">Statistical significance alone is not the same as operational importance.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How should an MLOps team handle Model Monitoring alerts using root-cause analysis, subgroup checks, safe deployment and rollback?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Incident response",
      "options": [
        "Investigate inputs, pipelines, outcomes and affected subgroups. Validate fixes on representative data and release gradually with clear ownership and rollback controls, rather than automatically retraining after every alert.",
        "Retrain automatically on all new production requests whenever drift appears, regardless of whether their true labels are known. Deploy immediately because newer examples always improve generalization to the current user population.",
        "Disable noisy alerts until the next release and roll back every model update without inspecting feature transformations or service faults. Previously passing offline evaluation removes the need to check the recovered deployment again.",
        "Close monitoring incidents when global accuracy and uptime are stable, even if smaller groups are failing. Teams can update the model using the current test set without separate release verification when overall metrics look healthy."
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> An alert should lead to investigation, not automatic retraining. Check logging, feature transformations, genuine performance, changing populations, service failures and subgroup impact. Once the cause is understood, validate a fix on representative data and use shadow evaluation or a controlled canary release with rollback ready. Imagine an early wildfire detection system: an unusual alert pattern deserves a safety review, since deploying an untested update could be worse than maintaining the current version. Keep incident owners and model versions documented.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mm-figure\"><span class=\"mm-kicker\">QUESTION 07 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mm-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mmh7 mmd7\"><title id=\"mmh7\">Investigate, validate, then release safely</title><desc id=\"mmd7\">Four steps show alert detection, root-cause and subgroup investigation, offline/shadow validation and controlled canary deployment with rollback.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#288573\">07 · MODEL MONITORING</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5367\">Investigate, validate, then release safely</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"113\" width=\"936\" height=\"265\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#4c7f92\">AN ALERT IS THE START OF AN INCIDENT WORKFLOW</text><rect x=\"52\" y=\"181\" width=\"208\" height=\"108\" fill=\"#eaf7fb\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"156\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#3c8197\">1. DETECT</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"262\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#53778a\">Score / drift signal</text><rect x=\"282\" y=\"181\" width=\"208\" height=\"108\" fill=\"#f0f3fd\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"386\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#6977a3\">2. TRIAGE</text><text x=\"386\" y=\"262\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#53778a\">Labels / root cause</text><rect x=\"512\" y=\"181\" width=\"208\" height=\"108\" fill=\"#eaf8f0\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#328b77\">3. VALIDATE</text><text x=\"616\" y=\"262\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#53778a\">Holdout / shadow</text><rect x=\"742\" y=\"181\" width=\"208\" height=\"108\" fill=\"#fff2e8\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" rx=\"13\"/><text x=\"846\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#b47b53\">4. DEPLOY</text><text x=\"846\" y=\"262\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#53778a\">Canary / rollback</text><line x1=\"262\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M268 226L278 235L268 244\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"492\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"508\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M498 226L508 235L498 244\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"722\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"738\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M728 226L738 235L728 244\" stroke=\"#5f9aa5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"336\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#547b8c\">Safeguards: subgroup checks · versioned logs · incident owner · rollback option</text></svg></div><p class=\"mm-note\">Detect, investigate, validate, release carefully and retain rollback controls.</p></section>"
    }
